SCRIPTGEN POLISH — CONTEXT LOG
Date: 2026-08-08
Scope: src/scriptgen/* (+ readme.md, tests/test_scriptgen_parts.py)
================================================================================

WHY THIS WORK HAPPENED
----------------------
scriptgen's job is to produce a *perfect* per-segment video prompt for literal
video-generation models (MiniMax H3 et al.), targeting short-form
Instagram/YouTube content. Review of the existing outputs under
films/rats/out/scripts and films/_clinicalclarity/out/scripts showed they were
"okay but dull": technically compliant (timecoded beats, blocking, expressions,
sound) but reading as moving postcards — slow push-in opens everywhere, no
scene-wide escalation, no hook, prompt dilution from too many rules, and files
exceeding the budget (e.g. frisby_visits_mr_ages_part2.md at 6,609 chars,
silently written).

BUDGET CONTRACT (critical — do not change without understanding)
----------------------------------------------------------------
- Video models accept at most 7,000 chars per prompt.
- The animator (src/animator/prompt.py) tacks ~1,000 chars of reference
  instructions/tags onto the FRONT of the saved script at generation time
  (<IMAGE_REF_N> tags, FIRST_FRAME/LAST_FRAME headers, background-plate
  instructions, begin/end-pose instructions).
- Therefore the saved part file is hard-capped at MAX_SCRIPT_CHARS = 6000
  (src/scriptgen/config.py). config.py documents this derivation in comments.
- MAX_SCRIPT_PROMPT_CHARS = MAX_SCRIPT_CHARS - 2000 is the limit the MODEL IS
  TOLD per segment body. It is deliberately lower than the real budget because
  models consistently overshoot stated limits by ~1,000-2,000 chars. The real
  check is always the rendered full-file length vs MAX_SCRIPT_CHARS in the
  render/retry loop in cli._generate_part — the told number only biases output.
- Oversized behavior CHANGED: after MAX_RETRIES (3) condense attempts,
  cli._generate_part now raises RuntimeError instead of writing an oversized
  file (the old code logged a warning and wrote anyway).

WHAT WAS BUILT (5 phases, Phase 5 validation removed by request — user tests
manually)
----------------------------------------------------------------
PHASE 1 — Budget enforcement & integrity
- src/scriptgen/api.py: fixed UTF-8 mojibake bug. OpenRouter SSE responses
  often omit a charset, so requests fell back to latin-1 and double-encoded
  every UTF-8 character (em dashes became "â", ° became "Â°") — that garbage
  flowed into saved scripts and then into video prompts. Fix: set
  response.encoding = "utf-8" on both streaming and non-streaming responses.
- src/scriptgen/config.py: budget constants documented per the contract above;
  values unchanged (6000 / 4000 / 3 retries).
- src/scriptgen/format.py: slimmed the saved-file template (this template is
  repeated in EVERY part file, so it competes with the shooting plan for
  budget). Dropped the redundant depth/eyeline MANDATES bullets (those rules
  live in the generation system instruction and the animator re-adds its own);
  kept the 3 anti-failure mandates (no teleporting; only declared speaker moves
  mouth; continuous secondary motion). KEPT the parse anchors other code
  depends on: "Characters appearing:" (animator/script.py
  parse_scene_characters), "=== SHARED SETTING & LIGHT" and "=== SCENE SCRIPT"
  markers (scriptgen/parse.py parse_part_file). NOTE: "Characters appearing:"
  and the "Match designs..." sentence are on SEPARATE LINES — merging them
  breaks parse_part_file's line-anchored regex (this was caught and fixed
  during build).
- src/scriptgen/parse.py: fixed latent bug where parse_part_file split the
  characters line on commas INSIDE <VOICE> tags; it now strips <VOICE>...</VOICE>
  before splitting.

PHASE 2 — Director's Treatment (whole-script planning; the biggest dullness fix)
- New pass 1: cli._generate_treatment runs BEFORE any part is generated.
  prompts.build_treatment_system_instruction + build_treatment_prompt plan the
  entire scene as one short film with EXACTLY these sections: Hook, Dramatic
  Question, Escalation Ladder (one bullet per segment), The Turn, Unforgettable
  Image, Dialogue Spine (5-8 lines with speaker + job tag), Final Held Frame.
  Treatment is kept ~600 chars.
- The treatment string is embedded in EVERY part prompt
  (build_part0_prompt / build_next_part_prompt both take a new `treatment`
  parameter — signature change; tests updated). Segment 0 must land the Hook;
  later segments must raise their rung on the ladder and serve the
  Unforgettable Image / Final Held Frame.

PHASE 3 — Instagram dialogue guide (deliberately NOT a dialogue cap)
- User decision: IG shorts squeeze lots of dialogue into 30s; too much was the
  problem, not dialogue itself. So prompts.py DIALOGUE CRAFT section now
  enforces volume + economy instead of a cap: ~50-70 spoken words per scene
  across 5-8 lines; max 8-10 words per line; one idea per line; the FINAL line
  is the shortest and hardest (the punch); "the deletion test" (a line that
  could be removed without changing the scene does not exist); each line does
  exactly one job — ASK / ANSWER / DEFLECT / WARN / REVEAL; every exchange
  shifts power/emotional balance; speak-in-action (every line paired with a
  visible physical act; the listener's body is half the scene); subtext over
  exposition; no invented backstory beyond the story beat.

PHASE 4 — Attention engineering system prompt
- prompts.build_system_instruction rewritten (~7,000 chars of rules condensed;
  now ~14k including roster/style injection, but rule-duplication removed).
  Core new sections:
  * ATTENTION ENGINEERING: hook-first opens (NEVER establishing wides or static
    frames in second one); ONE focal point per beat (brightest point / only
    moving thing / eyeline cue / story object); escalation across parts;
    plant-and-payoff micro-questions; the turn shifts camera+light+sound+music
    together; the unforgettable image gets a held beat.
  * LITERAL DIRECTION LANGUAGE: only observable physical facts; emotion ONLY
    as visible body action (no bare labels); simple literal camera words; NO
    invented numbers (no degrees/kelvin/inches/percentages — literal models
    ignore them); one camera move per segment, stillness is a deliberate choice.
  * TIME-CODED BEATS kept ([0:00-0:03] tiling the 10s).
  * SPATIAL & PHYSICAL LAWS: spatial mapping first sentence; one unbroken shot;
    continuous locomotion; feet on floor; shared depth plane for interaction;
    continuous secondary motion; never into lens; only speaker mouths move.
  * DIALOGUE CRAFT = the Phase 3 guide.
- Output format unchanged (title / Logline / Characters in Scene /
  Setting & Light / ## Segment N (span)) so scriptgen.parse and
  animator.script parsing still work; segment bodies remain self-contained.

PHASE 5 — Critique loop (modeled on blueprint_generator's reviewer pattern)
- prompts.build_critique_prompt: after each part draft, a critic scores 7 axes
  1-10 (hook, escalation, attention, dialogue economy, literalness,
  filmability, length) vs the treatment and returns ONE concrete fix per axis
  under 8.
- prompts.build_polish_prompt applies fixes in a single rewrite preserving
  structure/limits.
- cli._critique parses "SCORES:" / "FIXES:"; CRITIQUE_PASS_THRESHOLD = 8 (min
  score across axes). If all axes >= 8, no polish call is made. Exactly ONE
  polish rewrite max per part (no loop).

FLOW SUMMARY (cli.run)
----------------------
1. _generate_treatment(story, scene, parts, ...)        [1 LLM call]
2. per part idx:
   a. build_part0_prompt / build_next_part_prompt (treatment embedded)
   b. _generate                                            [1 LLM call]
   c. _critique                                            [1 LLM call]
   d. if fixes: polish via build_polish_prompt             [0-1 LLM call]
   e. render via format_segment_base_prompt; measure vs MAX_SCRIPT_CHARS
   f. if over: condense retry up to MAX_RETRIES            [0-3 LLM calls]
   g. still over: RuntimeError (hard fail; nothing written for that part)
3. prune obsolete part files beyond --parts.
Total API calls per scene: 1 + parts*(2..6). Default model qwen/qwen3.8-max,
reasoning effort medium, temperature 0.7 (unchanged).

TESTS (tests/test_scriptgen_parts.py rewritten; run via unittest, NOT pytest —
pytest is not installed in the venv)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Command: PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tests
- new tests: treatment passed to build_part0_prompt; oversized part raises
  instead of writing; critique fixes trigger exactly one polish call; passing
  scores skip polish; low scores yield fixes; budget constants.
- pre-existing failure unrelated to this work: tests/test_prompt.py
  test_build_initial_prompt (blueprint prompt checklist mismatch; fails on main
  too — left alone).

OUT OF SCOPE / KNOWN GAPS for future work
----------------------------------------------------------------
- No hand-written gold exemplar segment added to the system prompt yet (plan
  item from Phase 4; deferred — would teach shot-paragraph shape better than
  rules if outputs still read flat after manual testing).
- Critique threshold (8) and single polish pass are tunables in cli.py.
- Temperature 0.7 for drafts; could be raised to ~0.9 now that the critic
  constrains output, if user testing shows drafts too safe.
- Existing saved scripts under films/*/out/scripts are OLD FORMAT-ERA outputs;
  regenerate with --force to get treatment+critique behavior.
- readme.md section 4.B updated to describe treatment/critique/length/dialogue
  guide behavior.

USER PREFERENCES ESTABLISHED HERE (carry into future scriptgen work)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
- User tests video generation manually; NEVER run animator.py/scriptgen
  generation for them (also in AGENTS.md).
- Dialogue must stay plentiful but economical — do not re-introduce hard line
  caps; the craft guide (words-per-scene, words-per-line, one-job-per-line)
  is the mechanism.
- 7,000 absolute video-prompt ceiling and ~1,000 animator headroom are fixed
  constraints of the downstream models, not preferences.
