MINIMAX PROMPT-GUIDE ALIGNMENT — follow-up change set
Date: 2026-08-08 (same session, after the polish above)
Reference: MiniMax Video Prompt Writing Guide
(docs_VIDEO_PROMPT_WRITING_GUIDE_base_en.txt; original at
/mnt/storage/jdunlap/Downloads/)
================================================================================

WHY
---
The default video provider is MiniMax H3 (both `minimax` and `openrouter`
providers), and the guide specifies an exact prompt structure our free-form
part files did not follow. Phases 1-4 implemented; Phase 5 (multishot) is
deferred and documented in logs/scriptgen-multishot-proposal.log.

WHAT CHANGED
------------
PHASE 1 — Three core fields (src/scriptgen/format.py, prompts.py, parse.py)
- Saved part file structure is now: preamble (style/camera/scene/characters/
  MANDATES) → === SHARED SETTING & LIGHT === → segment body consisting of the
  three labeled fields:
    integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] 2D-animated, <style token>,
      <spatial mapping>. <timecoded beats...>
    overall_soundscape: <1-4 sentences>
    non_diegetic_music: <1-3 sentences, instrumentation/tempo/rhythm/dynamics
      only, no mood words; N/A allowed>
- The old "=== SCENE SCRIPT (story time ...) ===" marker is GONE. Parsing
  anchors now: extract_segment_body starts at the
  "integrated_multimodal_description:" line; parse_part_file's setting regex
  ends at that label. The `span` parameter of format_segment_base_prompt is
  retained for interface stability but no longer rendered (the animator owns
  clip duration).
- Sound split rule in the system prompt: synchronized diegetic sounds stay
  inline in beats; ambient/physical/non-verbal sounds consolidate into
  overall_soundscape; audience-only score goes to non_diegetic_music; music
  audible to characters is diegetic and stays inline.
- Single [Shot 1] per segment is mandatory (guide favors single shot for
  FL2VA interpolation; matches our frame-chaining). [0:00-0:03] pacing
  markers inside the shot are retained.

PHASE 2 — Camera vocabulary lock (prompts.py CAMERA MOTION VOCABULARY)
- The "simple literal camera words" rule was replaced by the guide's exact
  vocabulary: Zoom In/Out, Push In/Pull Out, Pan Left/Right, Truck Left/Right,
  Tilt Up/Down, Pedestal Up/Down, Arc Shot, Tracking Shot, Static Shot,
  Shake Slightly/Strongly, POV, Roll Clockwise/Counterclockwise, with
  optional "with small/large amplitude" and "at slow/fast speed", written as
  natural English actions.

PHASE 3 — Dialogue encoding (prompts.py SPEAKERS & DIALOGUE ENCODING;
animator/prompt.py tag protection)
- Speaker IDs (S1)/(S2) assigned in Characters-in-Scene order; identity
  phrase + ID + physical action + delivery OUTSIDE <d>, only
  "[English] <verbatim line>" INSIDE. This replaces the old
  `NAME: "line"` attribution rule (the DIALOGUE CRAFT Instagram guide stays
  otherwise unchanged: word budget, line jobs, deletion test, punch last).
- animator/prompt.py tag_character_mentions now protects <d>...</d> spans in
  addition to double-quoted spans (PROTECTED_SPAN_RE), so character names
  inside spoken lines never receive <IMAGE_REF_N> tags.

PHASE 4 — Alignment instructions (animator/prompt.py, animator/api.py)
- The old "[# Sources <FIRST_FRAME>IMAGE_REF_N]" / "[# Background scene use
  references ...]" prefix markers are REPLACED by the guide's exact sentences
  (build_alignment_instructions), prepended as the first line(s) of the final
  prompt:
  * opening frame only (I2VA, normal chained parts): "For the target video, at
    0.00 seconds into the target video, <IMAGE_REF_N> (from [Shot 1]) is fully
    referenced."
  * opening + closing (FL2VA, --force regen of a middle part): "How the
    reference pictures align with the target video — ... 0.00-second mark ...;
    ... S.SS-second mark ..." with S.SS = clip duration, two decimals.
  * closing only (L2VA, --frame-end): "... <IMAGE_REF_N> (from [Shot 1])
    aligns with the S.SS-second mark of the target video."
  * background plate: "The environment set of this video matches background
    reference <IMAGE_REF_N> exactly."
  The begin/held-final-pose instruction still follows when there is no
  opening frame. add_reference_tags gained a `duration` parameter (wired from
  args.duration in animator/cli.py).
- animator/api.py (Gemini provider) now labels continuity/closing frames
  <IMAGE_REF_N> with indices consistent with the prompt builder's numbering
  (characters → background → continuity → closing), so the alignment
  sentences reference the correct images for every provider.
- The ref-statement replacement in add_reference_tags targets the current
  template line "Match designs EXACTLY to reference images; never use
  references as opening frames." (old English removed).

TESTS
-----
- tests/test_prompt.py updated for the new alignment sentences; new test
  test_dialogue_blocks_are_not_tagged. All pass except the pre-existing
  unrelated test_build_initial_prompt failure.
- Smoke test verified end-to-end: format_segment_base_prompt output with the
  three fields parses via parse_part_file, animator parse_scene_characters,
  and build_direction; <d> blocks stay untagged.

COMPATIBILITY NOTES
-------------------
- OLD part files (pre-this-change, "=== SCENE SCRIPT" format) still animate:
  animator treats the whole file as the segment body and prepends alignment
  instructions; extract_segment_body falls back to the whole text. But their
  inline Sound:/Music: lines and NAME: "line" dialogue don't follow the new
  encoding — regenerate scenes with --force for best results.
- The treatment pass, critique pass, budget contract, and IG dialogue guide
  from the earlier polish are unchanged by this work.
